## Why This Matters

Modern AI agent systems reason about security but enforce decisions in software. This creates a fundamental gap:

```
AI agent decides: "This request looks suspicious — block it"
            ↓
Writes to an in-memory blocklist
            ↓
Blocklist lives in the same process space as the agent
            ↓
A sufficiently privileged attacker can modify the blocklist
            ↓
The AI's security decision is overruled by software
```

No matter how sophisticated the reasoning — if enforcement is software, enforcement can be bypassed by software.

Hardware closes this gap permanently:

```
AI agent decides: "This request looks suspicious — block it"
            ↓
Calls hardware tool — ASIC enforces at silicon level
            ↓
No software process can override what silicon decided
            ↓
The AI's security decision is hardware-rooted
```

