## Decision Flow Examples

### Example 1 — Network Anomaly Response

```
Watchdog agent: "Unknown MAC address detected — 3 times in 60 seconds"
        ↓
LLM receives proposal
        ↓
LLM calls verify_request_pow(challenge, solution, difficulty)
        ↓
ASIC verifies → valid
        ↓
LLM calls hardware_rate_check("unknown_mac_alerts", "block_request")
        ↓
ASIC returns → {allowed: true, remaining: 4}
        ↓
LLM reasons:
    "Three unknown MAC alerts in 60 seconds is anomalous.
     PoW verified. Rate limit not exceeded.
     Recommend: alert human, do not auto-block yet.
     Confidence: medium — could be a new legitimate device."
        ↓
Human receives alert with LLM reasoning attached
        ↓
Human approves or denies with Ed25519 signature from vault
        ↓
If approved: watchdog executes, logs result
```

### Example 2 — Model Load Request

```
Inference request received for model "codellama-13b-q4"
        ↓
LLM receives load request
        ↓
LLM calls verify_model_integrity(
    "/models/codellama-13b-q4.gguf",
    vault_reference["codellama-13b-q4"]
)
        ↓
ASIC streams 8GB model file, computes Scrypt hash
        ↓
Hash matches vault reference → True
        ↓
LLM reasons:
    "Model integrity verified by hardware.
     Hash matches vault reference.
     Safe to proceed with inference."
        ↓
Model loads — inference proceeds
        ↓
If hash had NOT matched:
    LLM reasons:
        "Hardware integrity check failed.
         Model weights do not match vault reference.
         This model may have been tampered with.
         Refusing to load. Alerting human immediately."
    Model does not load — alert fires
```

### Example 3 — Key Generation

```
WireGuard peer rotation requested
        ↓
LLM determines new keypair needed
        ↓
LLM calls get_hardware_entropy(bytes_needed=64)
        ↓
ASIC returns 64 bytes of hardware entropy
        ↓
LLM uses entropy as seed for key generation
        ↓
Keys generated with hardware-quality randomness
        ↓
No software PRNG involved in the critical random step
```

