## This Is Not Running LLM On ASIC

This document describes a different concept from running neural network inference on hashing silicon (see <hash-native-ai.md>).

```
Running LLM ON ASIC:
    → Neural network weights computed by hashing silicon
    → Hash-native neural architecture
    → Long-term research direction
    → Requires new model architectures
    → Hardware: KHeavyHash most promising near-term

LLM USING ASIC as tool:
    → Standard LLM (any model) calls hardware via tool API
    → No changes to model architecture needed
    → Implementable TODAY with existing hardware
    → Hardware: any Scrypt/SHA256/Blake3 ASIC with controller access
    → THIS DOCUMENT
```

Both concepts are worth pursuing. They are complementary, not competing. The tool-use pattern is achievable now. The native architecture is the longer horizon.

