## Hardware Agnosticism

This pattern works with any cryptographic ASIC that can expose a local API. The specific algorithm determines which tools are most natural:

|Algorithm |Most Natural Tool Application                            |
|----------|---------------------------------------------------------|
|Scrypt    |PoW gating (memory-hard = expensive to fake)             |
|SHA-256   |Model integrity (Merkle tree verification)               |
|Blake3    |High-throughput streaming hash (large model verification)|
|KHeavyHash|PoW + rate limiting (SHA-3 core)                         |
|Ethash    |Memory-hard verification (DAG properties)                |

The LangChain tool interface is identical regardless of underlying algorithm. Swap the ASIC, update the tool implementation, the agent reasoning layer is unchanged.

