## Security Properties

### What This Architecture Provides

```
1. Hardware-rooted request authentication
   LLM cannot be tricked into approving a request
   that hasn't cleared hardware PoW verification

2. Hardware-rooted model integrity
   LLM cannot reason about a model that hasn't
   cleared hardware hash verification

3. Hardware-quality entropy
   LLM cannot generate weak keys because
   entropy source is hardware not software PRNG

4. Hardware-enforced rate limits
   LLM cannot be overwhelmed by request floods
   because hardware counters cannot be reset by software

5. Fail-closed by design
   If hardware is unreachable all tools return False/None
   LLM system prompt instructs rejection on any hardware failure
   No action proceeds without hardware confirmation
```

### What This Architecture Does Not Provide

```
1. Protection against physical ASIC compromise
   Physical access to the ASIC breaks the model

2. Protection if the LLM itself is compromised
   A backdoored model could ignore tool results
   Mitigated by: model integrity verification before load

3. Absolute latency guarantees
   Hardware round-trip adds milliseconds per tool call
   Acceptable for security-critical paths

4. Protection against quantum attacks
   Scrypt and Ed25519 are not quantum-resistant
   Post-quantum migration is a future concern
```

