## Implementation Pattern

### Minimal Viable Implementation

```
1. Any ASIC with local API access (see ScryptGate)
2. Any LLM accessible via Ollama or API
3. LangChain with tool registration (shown above)
4. Four tool functions (shown above)
5. System prompt instructing hardware-first verification

That is the complete pattern.
No special hardware beyond the ASIC.
No special model architecture.
No custom training.
```

### Production Hardening

```
1. mTLS between LLM server and ASIC API
   → Prevent MITM on local network
   
2. Tool call logging to immutable append-only log
   → Every hardware call recorded with timestamp
   
3. Hardware health monitoring
   → Alert if ASIC unreachable before requests arrive
   
4. Tool result caching with TTL
   → Don't re-verify the same PoW token twice
   → Cache model hash for model load duration only
   
5. Separate tool execution process
   → Tool calls run in isolated process
   → Compromised tool cannot affect LLM process
```

