## Comparison With Existing Approaches

|Approach               |Reasoning     |Enforcement|Hardware-Rooted|Cost       |
|-----------------------|--------------|-----------|---------------|-----------|
|Software firewall rules|❌ Static rules|Software   |❌ No           |Low        |
|LLM + software security|✅ Adaptive    |Software   |❌ No           |Medium     |
|HSM + software logic   |❌ No reasoning|Hardware   |✅ Yes          |High ($$$) |
|TPM + software logic   |❌ Limited     |Hardware   |✅ Yes          |Medium     |
|**LLM + ASIC tools**   |✅ Adaptive    |Hardware   |✅ Yes          |**Low ($)**|

The LLM + ASIC tool pattern is the only approach in this table that provides both adaptive reasoning AND hardware enforcement at consumer hardware cost.

